Red → green evidence follows. Every red Rust result below is a running-test
assertion failure (exit 101), not a compiler error. Red gate tests exit 1.
Where the original product already enforced the boundary, an explicit fault
control supplies the red witness. scripts/hardening-controls.py restores exact
source bytes in finally and checks the restored hash before running green.
The Rust green command for all rows is the exit-0 all-targets command above;
the named witness is visible in make-test-green.log. Control rows additionally
record the exact filtered red and green commands and exits in their JSON files.

1. Bound cancellation drain. src/process.rs:162-165 establishes a 500 ms drain
   deadline after TERM/KILL/reap and closes the read handles at the deadline.
   tests/cancel_process.rs:120 runs a real setsid pipe holder (portable Python
   setsid fixture on macOS) and asserts TurnEnded{Cancelled} in under 2 seconds.
   Red: cargo test --offline --locked --test cancel_process escaped_pipe_holder_cannot_stall_a_cancelled_turn → 101.
   Green: the same witness passed in the all-targets command → 0.
   Evidence: hardening/item01-drain-red.{json,log}; make-test-green.log.

2. Reaped group ownership. src/process.rs:31-60 records unreaped ownership and
   disables all group signals after wait reaps the child. Drop uses the same
   guard. The unit signaller records calls without signalling an arbitrary OS
   pgid. The original unconditional Drop path, minimally instrumented with
   that signaller, failed the running unit test.
   Red: cargo test --offline --locked --lib reaped_group_drop_never_signals_a_reused_identity → 101.
   Green: process::ownership_tests::reaped_group_drop_never_signals_a_reused_identity passed → 0.
   Evidence: hardening/item02-owner-red.{json,log}.

3. Nonvacuous birth fence. tests/formal/models.rs:147 captures a completion's
   generation when held and compares it with the current generation before
   apply. tests/formal_nonvacuity.rs:24 proves a later tag is reachable, A→B→A
   retains A's completion and all correct states have bad=0. Removing the apply
   guard fails safety in both backends (66 states / 96 edges in the control).
   Red: cargo test --offline --locked --test formal_nonvacuity → 101 on the old model.
   Green: formal_nonvacuity plus Native/Parity → 0.
   Evidence: hardening/item03-04-model-red.{json,log}; HarnessCancelTree metadata.

